(7347538, 1148458, 113591, '<td valign="top">Probably not enough eye-candy.<br/> <br/>I do think it is a reasonably well balanced shot, exactly the one that should be used in the History text books, or Google. It displays the monuments in good colouor and perfect definition, it places them in their right perspective, and there are some nice lines formed by the horison, trees and paving.<br/> <br/>The clouds are a bit dull. The cannon is perhaps too close to the left side of the image.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Probably not enough eye-candy. I do think it is a reasonably well balanced shot, exactly the one that should be used in the History text books, or Google. It displays the monuments in good colouor and perfect definition, it places them in their right perspective, and there are some nice lines formed by the horison, trees and paving. The clouds are a bit dull. The cannon is perhaps too close to the left side of the image. ', '2015-05-04 09:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347539, 1148427, 109227, '<td valign="top">Great job on this one; my top pick.</td>', 'Great job on this one; my top pick.', '2015-05-04 09:09:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347540, 1148186, 109227, '<td valign="top">Love the human presence here, it helps tell the story.  Congrats.</td>', 'Love the human presence here, it helps tell the story.  Congrats.', '2015-05-04 09:10:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347541, 1148480, 109227, '<td valign="top">Loved the composition on this one.  Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Loved the composition on this one.  Congrats on the ribbon.', '2015-05-04 09:11:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347542, 1148458, 61679, '<td valign="top">Since I''m not a paying member, I couldn''t vote on this image.  But if I did I would have given it a 5, as it clearly meets the challenge.  There are two things that bother me about this image.<br/> <br/>1.  The light doesn''t look balanced.  The background has a bunch of detail but the face of the soldier has very little.  Since the soldier and background are basically facing the same direction, my eye expects about the same amount of detail.  As is, the background looks over processed.<br/> <br/>2.  The crop is a little tight for my taste.  A bit more space on the bottom and sides would have given the monument more breathing room and better convey the size of the battle field.  <br/> <br/>As is, it is a monument shot with the background being dominate.<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Since I''m not a paying member, I couldn''t vote on this image.  But if I did I would have given it a 5, as it clearly meets the challenge.  There are two things that bother me about this image. 1.  The light doesn''t look balanced.  The background has a bunch of detail but the face of the soldier has very little.  Since the soldier and background are basically facing the same direction, my eye expects about the same amount of detail.  As is, the background looks over processed. 2.  The crop is a little tight for my taste.  A bit more space on the bottom and sides would have given the monument more breathing room and better convey the size of the battle field.   As is, it is a monument shot with the background being dominate. Tim', '2015-05-04 09:19:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347544, 1147987, 12611, '<td valign="top">Absolute ribbon hound. all over the front page and rightly so. Excellent choice of burned copper/sepia for this.</td>', 'Absolute ribbon hound. all over the front page and rightly so. Excellent choice of burned copper/sepia for this.', '2015-05-04 09:43:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347545, 1148480, 12611, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition. It takes only a few years, in the modern era, to achieve the state of disrepair(in our statues)that it took the Greeks ages to accomplish...</td>', 'Excellent composition. It takes only a few years, in the modern era, to achieve the state of disrepair(in our statues)that it took the Greeks ages to accomplish...', '2015-05-04 09:44:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347546, 1148186, 12611, '<td valign="top">Very touching entry, without being overly contrived- that isn''t easy to do, so kudos and congrats.</td>', 'Very touching entry, without being overly contrived- that isn''t easy to do, so kudos and congrats.', '2015-05-04 09:45:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347547, 1148027, 12611, '<td valign="top">Absolutely perfect, seems like a super trip!</td>', 'Absolutely perfect, seems like a super trip!', '2015-05-04 09:47:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347548, 1148343, 12611, '<td valign="top">Stunningly futurist. all the "natural splendor" of man made lights and night.</td>', 'Stunningly futurist. all the "natural splendor" of man made lights and night.', '2015-05-04 09:48:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347549, 1148362, 12611, '<td valign="top">Entries for Naples, entries form Venice... how convenient! Nicely composed and presented, as well.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-05-04 08:50:13.</i></td>', 'Entries for Naples, entries form Venice... how convenient! Nicely composed and presented, as well.', '2015-05-04 09:50:01.000000', '2015-05-04 09:50:13.000000', 0),
(7347551, 1148481, 12611, '<td valign="top">This one was great Mark- definitely one of the best here. Great job of "presenting" the monument effortlessly with a fitting and stunning background.</td>', 'This one was great Mark- definitely one of the best here. Great job of "presenting" the monument effortlessly with a fitting and stunning background.', '2015-05-04 09:51:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347553, 1148413, 12611, '<td valign="top">great light for this shot, given what you had to work with.</td>', 'great light for this shot, given what you had to work with.', '2015-05-04 09:55:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347554, 1148231, 12611, '<td valign="top">Impressive and moving.</td>', 'Impressive and moving.', '2015-05-04 09:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347555, 1148458, 77196, '<td valign="top">FWIW - Considering my scores, what do I know, but my thoughts...<br/>It is a busy picture - lots of rocks, bushes, etc. in the background. <br/>The tree line seems to have a light border between it and the sky (result of processing, I''d guess)<br/>To me, the biggest problem is that the cannon is pointing out of the picture to the left. It would work if the cannon was on the other side of the statue, or if there was some space for the cannon to point into. <br/>I think this monument would have worked better photographically if you''d included only the cannon or the statue, but not both. Maybe there is a better angle that would "condense" the elements - making them appear closer together. <br/>I think this is an excellent example of a historical group placing things with no thought of photography. Here''s a cannon. Here''s a statue. How we place them doesn''t matter. With a little thought, a better arrangement could have been used making the scene more memorable and accessible. <br/>You have some very nice color / texture in the ground cover. <br/></td>', 'FWIW - Considering my scores, what do I know, but my thoughts...It is a busy picture - lots of rocks, bushes, etc. in the background. The tree line seems to have a light border between it and the sky (result of processing, I''d guess)To me, the biggest problem is that the cannon is pointing out of the picture to the left. It would work if the cannon was on the other side of the statue, or if there was some space for the cannon to point into. I think this monument would have worked better photographically if you''d included only the cannon or the statue, but not both. Maybe there is a better angle that would "condense" the elements - making them appear closer together. I think this is an excellent example of a historical group placing things with no thought of photography. Here''s a cannon. Here''s a statue. How we place them doesn''t matter. With a little thought, a better arrangement could have been used making the scene more memorable and accessible. You have some very nice color / texture in the ground cover. ', '2015-05-04 09:56:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347556, 1148480, 40391, '<td valign="top">Great photo and congrats on the ribbon. All you need is a Red on the next challenge and you''ll have the trifecta.</td>', 'Great photo and congrats on the ribbon. All you need is a Red on the next challenge and you''ll have the trifecta.', '2015-05-04 09:56:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347557, 1148214, 12611, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully presented.</td>', 'Wonderfully presented.', '2015-05-04 09:56:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347558, 1148322, 12611, '<td valign="top">Super. No regrets. One of the best photographs in the challenge.</td>', 'Super. No regrets. One of the best photographs in the challenge.', '2015-05-04 09:58:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347559, 1148458, 100831, '<td valign="top">This is a good shot of the battleground, ok for the composition. I gave it a 6 because the lack of contrast in colors and lighting leaves it a bit dull looking, overall.</td>', 'This is a good shot of the battleground, ok for the composition. I gave it a 6 because the lack of contrast in colors and lighting leaves it a bit dull looking, overall.', '2015-05-04 10:00:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347561, 1148486, 12611, '<td valign="top">Lots of good stuff going on here. (The guy in the overalls looks like Mykelti Williamson playing Ellstin Limehouse in the TV series Justified.)</td>', 'Lots of good stuff going on here. (The guy in the overalls looks like Mykelti Williamson playing Ellstin Limehouse in the TV series Justified.)', '2015-05-04 10:01:59.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(7347563, 1148458, 156466, '<td valign="top">Sometimes HDR is your friend, sometimes it''s not.  Here, it''s not.<br/> <br/>The textures and details of the background do nothing for you here, and if nothing else they pull the eye away from what''s supposed to be subject of your image.  There are more details in the rocks than there are in face of the statue.  Tack onto that the over structured and over-pinked look you can get from some HDR programs (I''m thinking this has HDR Efex Pro 2 written all over it) and it''s a quick and easy 5 for me. <br/> <br/>Composition is sound and all, but there''s nothing really interesting here and I''m no fan of the processing.  Frankly, I''m more interested in what''s next to the statue''s elbow than anything in the foreground.</td>', 'Sometimes HDR is your friend, sometimes it''s not.  Here, it''s not. The textures and details of the background do nothing for you here, and if nothing else they pull the eye away from what''s supposed to be subject of your image.  There are more details in the rocks than there are in face of the statue.  Tack onto that the over structured and over-pinked look you can get from some HDR programs (I''m thinking this has HDR Efex Pro 2 written all over it) and it''s a quick and easy 5 for me.  Composition is sound and all, but there''s nothing really interesting here and I''m no fan of the processing.  Frankly, I''m more interested in what''s next to the statue''s elbow than anything in the foreground.', '2015-05-04 10:03:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347566, 1147987, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by blindjustice:</b></div><hr/><i> Absolute ribbon hound. all over the front page and rightly so. Excellent choice of burned copper/sepia for this. </i></td></tr></table>. Hehe, don''t worry I promise to be quiet for at least a week :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by blindjustice: Absolute ribbon hound. all over the front page and rightly so. Excellent choice of burned copper/sepia for this. . Hehe, don''t worry I promise to be quiet for at least a week :-)', '2015-05-04 10:23:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347567, 1148322, 19825, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done, Johanna. I love the vast expanse and the hoop and lone figure. This finished much higher in my rankings.</td>', 'Very nicely done, Johanna. I love the vast expanse and the hoop and lone figure. This finished much higher in my rankings.', '2015-05-04 10:45:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347569, 1148214, 19825, '<td valign="top">Nicely done, Margaret. This finished much higher in my list.</td>', 'Nicely done, Margaret. This finished much higher in my list.', '2015-05-04 10:47:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347570, 1148480, 19825, '<td valign="top">Love the tones and composition of this. Excellent shot.</td>', 'Love the tones and composition of this. Excellent shot.', '2015-05-04 10:48:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347571, 1148458, 30049, '<td valign="top">Appreciate the feedback.  Yes, used HDR in PSP X7.  I thought it was pretty well balanced and I backed off on it''s impact (thank goodness).  :-)<br/> <br/>As for focus - the face of the statue is what it is ... no more detail available.  If you look at the base of the monument, the plaque, the concrete, etc... it''s all tack sharp, as is the Cannon.  That was the focal plane.  Thought I had that part correct at least ...</td>', 'Appreciate the feedback.  Yes, used HDR in PSP X7.  I thought it was pretty well balanced and I backed off on it''s impact (thank goodness).  :-) As for focus - the face of the statue is what it is ... no more detail available.  If you look at the base of the monument, the plaque, the concrete, etc... it''s all tack sharp, as is the Cannon.  That was the focal plane.  Thought I had that part correct at least ...', '2015-05-04 10:50:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347576, 1148027, 63218, '<td valign="top">he sky seems heavy--&amp; I discovered thru this pic that it is possible to homogenize with PP so that the light in Venice, Italy looks just the same as the light in Venice, Florida, which is good I guess or people wouldn''t be doing it</td>', 'he sky seems heavy--& I discovered thru this pic that it is possible to homogenize with PP so that the light in Venice, Italy looks just the same as the light in Venice, Florida, which is good I guess or people wouldn''t be doing it', '2015-05-04 10:54:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347591, 1148458, 159723, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I agree with the two issues raised by atupdate/Tim. I''ll add one more thing. To me the image looks cluttered, in lack of better words. This is because of everything going on in the hillside. All of the rocks, shrubs and different coloured grass is stealing my attention away from the actual monument. Of course this is not something you can do anything about, but perhaps a different angle might have done the monument more justice? I don''t know..I''m still learning :)<br/> <br/>Update: Oh..someone beat me to it. Note to self, refresh window before leaving a comment an hour before the initial viewing of the image<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-05-04 10:10:39.</i></td>', 'I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I agree with the two issues raised by atupdate/Tim. I''ll add one more thing. To me the image looks cluttered, in lack of better words. This is because of everything going on in the hillside. All of the rocks, shrubs and different coloured grass is stealing my attention away from the actual monument. Of course this is not something you can do anything about, but perhaps a different angle might have done the monument more justice? I don''t know..I''m still learning :) Update: Oh..someone beat me to it. Note to self, refresh window before leaving a comment an hour before the initial viewing of the image', '2015-05-04 11:07:54.000000', '2015-05-04 11:10:39.000000', 0),
(7347595, 1148480, 113016, '<td valign="top">thanks for the nice words everyone. <br/>In reviewing the original to send in... it reminded me that I removed some wires-- but also a protruding portion of the flagpole.<br/>I viewed it as incidental at the time...but in re-looking I honestly don''t think it is.  Bummer.... :o)  <br/> <br/></td>', 'thanks for the nice words everyone. In reviewing the original to send in... it reminded me that I removed some wires-- but also a protruding portion of the flagpole.I viewed it as incidental at the time...but in re-looking I honestly don''t think it is.  Bummer.... :o)   ', '2015-05-04 11:18:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347597, 1148458, 118154, '<td valign="top">Processing is way ott for this type of image and the composition is boring in the extreme.</td>', 'Processing is way ott for this type of image and the composition is boring in the extreme.', '2015-05-04 11:19:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347599, 1148458, 121949, '<td valign="top">As others have stated the background is competing with the subject. I would have used a shallower DOF and made the monument more the focal point. Or maybe Just chosen one of the objects. Looks like you have several different subjects in this photo and the viewer just doesn''t know where to focus.</td>', 'As others have stated the background is competing with the subject. I would have used a shallower DOF and made the monument more the focal point. Or maybe Just chosen one of the objects. Looks like you have several different subjects in this photo and the viewer just doesn''t know where to focus.', '2015-05-04 11:22:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7347600, 1148427, 113016, '<td valign="top">i was wrong on this image.  I didn''t score it very high (5), but in re-looking I was completely wrong. <br/>I love the clouds on this this.  And Johanna says it best below in that they bring the ''mighty'' to the monument.  <br/>Congrats on the blue!!</td>', 'i was wrong on this image.  I didn''t score it very high (5), but in re-looking I was completely wrong. I love the clouds on this this.  And Johanna says it best below in that they bring the ''mighty'' to the monument.  Congrats on the blue!!', '2015-05-04 11:24:40.000000', NULL, 0),
