(7347717, 1148027, 63218, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pixelpig:</b></div><hr/><i> he sky seems heavy--&amp; I discovered thru this pic that it is possible to homogenize with PP so that the light in Venice, Italy looks just the same as the light in Venice, Florida, which is good I guess or people wouldn''t be doing it </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Is there a different sun for Italy? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well I didn''t mean to come off all opinionated and all. It''s just that sunlight is different at different times of the year and in different locations. I just discovered for myself that HDR kind of standardizes the quality of the light/colors. Sorry if I offended anyone!</td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: Originally posted by pixelpig: he sky seems heavy--& I discovered thru this pic that it is possible to homogenize with PP so that the light in Venice, Italy looks just the same as the light in Venice, Florida, which is good I guess or people wouldn''t be doing it   Is there a different sun for Italy?   Well I didn''t mean to come off all opinionated and all. It''s just that sunlight is different at different times of the year and in different locations. I just discovered for myself that HDR kind of standardizes the quality of the light/colors. Sorry if I offended anyone!', '2015-05-04 18:07:59.000000', NULL, 0),
